- Insertion-only hunks use the unified-diff zero-length range position, while replacement/deletion retain consuming-range semantics. New-range positions are now authenticated against emitted output, so hashes cannot seal source at a different patch location.
- `DiscoveryExposureProof` carries both exact fold identities, including bundle, universe, benchmark, warmup, sessions digest/count, and endpoints, plus the complete shared reservation metadata. The comparison factory must match independently supplied expected identities and metadata before provider serialization.
