Both 30,000-byte candidates independently derive their cumulative unified diff and compact canonical source bundle and prove it remains within 64 KiB. The backslash candidate is the true maximum escaping case and fails closed with `next_context_oversize`; the equal-raw Unicode candidate fits because its UTF-8 is emitted without expansion. The existing 10,000-byte/45,000-byte ASCII cases continue to prove fitting and overflowing exact envelopes.

